Z||000000||jch82||04-08-2001||01:09 AM||||My 85GT doesnt have a sunroof but I would really like one. I have the entire interior out right now so I figure now would be the time to put one in.....How difficult is it to take off the roof out of a fiero? <P>There is already a hole cut for a sunroof so if I found a different roof (with sunroof), could I just swap the roofs? Or isn't it that easy? <P>From looking at my fiero, it seems like all that holds the roof down is a bunch of bolts and it would seem that I just have to unbolt both roofs and switch them. Thanks<P>Are all the roofs (84-88) interchangeable? I thought they were but thought I would ask just to be on the safe side. Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-08-2001||01:18 AM||||yea they are. but you have to cut it out around the 'a" pillars and back window, its full of this black tar like goo. Its not that big a deal, but def apita. Dont get any of the goo on upholstery, its really tough to get out. Prob gonna have to redo headliner too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||jch82||04-08-2001||01:22 AM||||Thanks, I am going to see about getting the roof out of my car tomorrow after work. I'll let you know how it all worked out. <P>I already have the headliner out and it is still in one piece (couldnt believe it).....<P>Any idea on where I should get the fabric to redo the headliner? Also what glue should I use for it? <P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||04-08-2001||01:29 AM||||It's not all too hard. I did mine in an afternoon. The hard part is finding someone with a undamaged roof panel. the front pillars usually break when it comes off. To take the old one off, pull out the headliner and there are about 8 bolts holding the roof skin on, and another half dozen or so under the windshield wiper linkage cover up front. There is that black goo under the pillars and the front of the roof panel above the windshield. To cut thruogh that, you'll need a little piano wire wrapped around to pieces of wood for handles. you feed the wire underneath the pillars then use the handles to drag it back and forth to cut through the goo until it's free. I think Paul Vargyus has a couple complete sunroof roof panels with glass and headliner. That's where I got mine, all for $150||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||04-08-2001||01:31 AM||||You cut the goo around the sides with piano wire..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_wind_1.jpg"> <P>Then the top...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/top_three.jpg"> <P>And.......we have LIFT OFF!!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/top_off.jpg">  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||04-08-2001||03:46 AM||||You need to get the headliner from the sunroof car. If I remember correctly you cannot use your original. To recover the headliner, see the headliner post under the "General" section. <BR>Be very very careful when removing the sunroof roof or yours (if you want to save it) The A-pillar section will crack easily.||||reg||1
